WEBVTT

00:43.376 --> 00:48.506
DOONA!

02:47.417 --> 02:50.170
EPISODE 5
MEANINGLESS KISS

03:23.036 --> 03:24.537
What was our assignment again?

03:24.621 --> 03:27.165
- Oh, hey.
- Hey, you're here.

03:29.792 --> 03:31.419
- I'll be off, then.
- Bye.

03:51.314 --> 03:52.148
Hi.

03:58.154 --> 04:00.114
Could I talk to you for a second?

04:02.283 --> 04:03.117
Sure.

04:03.660 --> 04:04.494
Go ahead.

04:11.709 --> 04:12.710
About what?

04:19.467 --> 04:22.011
Was it touching you? Sorry.

04:24.264 --> 04:25.723
Why did you do that yesterday?

04:25.807 --> 04:26.766
Yesterday?

04:31.938 --> 04:33.231
We kissed yesterday.

04:37.110 --> 04:37.944
I just did it.

04:38.945 --> 04:40.863
What other reason is there
to kiss someone?

04:41.614 --> 04:43.783
Why? Was it not very good?

04:48.371 --> 04:49.497
Do you like me?

04:50.915 --> 04:52.125
Do you?

04:56.963 --> 04:58.631
See? You don't.

04:59.674 --> 05:01.592
I don't kiss my friends.

05:03.094 --> 05:07.890
So let's not do anything
other than what we can do as friends.

05:10.018 --> 05:13.104
Wanting comfort from someone
because you're lonely

05:13.187 --> 05:15.106
and going through a rough time,
I get that.

05:16.190 --> 05:18.359
But that feeling can fool you.

05:18.985 --> 05:20.486
You'll get hurt that way.

05:22.280 --> 05:23.114
Hey,

05:24.615 --> 05:25.825
you're such a bore.

05:27.201 --> 05:30.538
You're all of 21 years old.
Why do you take everything so seriously?

05:33.166 --> 05:34.959
It's not like I asked you to be lovers.

05:35.460 --> 05:36.919
It gave me butterflies.

05:40.965 --> 05:43.801
And I don't want to feel that way
over something meaningless.

05:45.553 --> 05:47.305
It's okay to get butterflies from me.

05:48.723 --> 05:52.018
Everyone does and then gets over it.
You think you're any different?

06:20.463 --> 06:24.425
SEEKING FEMALE ROOMMATE
FOR FIRST FLOOR OF SHARED HOUSE

06:38.106 --> 06:41.067
Excuse me! Could you hold
the elevator for me? Wait!

06:42.276 --> 06:43.277
Wait!

06:45.321 --> 06:46.572
Oh, thank you!

06:46.656 --> 06:48.282
So sorry!

06:48.366 --> 06:50.743
- Thank you.
- Jeez, you could have taken the next one.

06:54.539 --> 06:56.541
- The kissing king!
- The samba girl?

06:56.624 --> 06:58.418
Yes, it's me, the samba girl!

06:58.501 --> 07:01.003
Yes, it's me! This is crazy!

07:01.754 --> 07:04.549
- Where are you going? To a lecture?
- No, I'm…

07:04.632 --> 07:07.844
Oh, I'll contact you
to give you the details.

07:07.927 --> 07:09.846
- I'll contact you in a bit!
- Yeah, sure.

07:09.929 --> 07:10.888
Thank you.

07:16.185 --> 07:18.813
- Let me crash in your room for a bit.
- I'm off.

07:20.273 --> 07:21.107
Honey!

07:21.899 --> 07:24.485
You piece of trash! Get out of my sight!

07:27.447 --> 07:30.241
- What do I do?
- Hey.

07:32.660 --> 07:34.912
I've been kicked out of my dorm.

07:34.996 --> 07:36.622
Can't you help me out?

07:45.798 --> 07:47.550
About what you said to me last time.

07:47.633 --> 07:50.261
You mean when I told you
about my feelings for you?

07:51.637 --> 07:52.638
Yes.

07:53.222 --> 07:55.224
I want to give you my answer.

07:55.349 --> 07:56.726
You can take your time.

07:57.852 --> 07:59.520
I feel like I know what's coming.

08:00.646 --> 08:02.690
I have feelings for someone else.

08:05.234 --> 08:07.862
- If I gave you mixed signals--
- You mean Won-jun?

08:12.867 --> 08:16.496
You never gave me mixed signals.
I knew. I just chose to ignore it.

08:19.624 --> 08:20.583
I'm sorry.

08:23.044 --> 08:25.129
LITERARY SOCIETY
SPARK

08:45.191 --> 08:49.320
MOVING OUT? YOU'RE PENNILESS. COME HOME,
OR I WON'T SUPPORT YOU EVER AGAIN

08:52.823 --> 08:55.535
I'M AT THE PARKING LOT
GET OVER HERE AS SOON AS YOU'RE DONE

08:55.618 --> 08:58.079
HAVE YOU FINALLY LOST IT?
HOW DARE YOU IGNORE MY CALLS?

08:58.162 --> 09:01.207
MOM SAYS YOU WORK PART-TIME. STUDY MORE,
DON'T HANG OUT LIKE A SLUT. REPLY!

09:08.839 --> 09:15.846
GOODBYE

09:18.766 --> 09:21.519
DAD
BLOCK CONTACT

09:32.572 --> 09:33.614
Won-jun.

09:49.297 --> 09:51.924
What is this place? It's pretty.

09:52.008 --> 09:52.842
Hey.

09:53.926 --> 09:55.177
Come over here.

09:56.846 --> 09:58.764
You can see your place from here too.

09:59.640 --> 10:01.892
I didn't know
there was an open rooftop here.

10:02.476 --> 10:03.894
There's a lot you don't know.

10:12.111 --> 10:13.779
What are you thinking about?

10:14.780 --> 10:15.740
Just that

10:15.823 --> 10:19.535
there are so many buildings out there,
but not one belongs to me.

10:19.619 --> 10:22.997
- I guess we're all the same.
- No, not you.

10:26.208 --> 10:27.376
Why not me?

10:27.918 --> 10:29.712
I didn't mean anything by it.

10:30.630 --> 10:33.466
I just didn't think
that's something you'd worry about.

10:36.177 --> 10:37.011
Jin-ju.

10:39.930 --> 10:42.350
Stop acting like you know me.

10:52.276 --> 10:53.778
What's wrong?

10:54.779 --> 10:57.073
Is there something I'm missing about you?

11:11.879 --> 11:12.797
I'm sorry.

11:15.966 --> 11:18.344
This wasn't what I wanted to talk about.

11:19.637 --> 11:21.305
I'm being such a nuisance.

12:07.518 --> 12:09.061
Don't drift too far away.

12:12.481 --> 12:14.191
That's all I wanted to say.

12:15.651 --> 12:17.903
Please don't let anything else happen.

12:18.904 --> 12:20.239
I can't take anymore.

12:33.085 --> 12:37.047
Hey, everyone! I, Choi I-ra, am moving!

12:49.268 --> 12:51.312
Yay! Forward, backward!

12:51.395 --> 12:53.522
To the left, to the right!

12:53.606 --> 12:55.775
- Isn't that Cute Guy?
- Where?

12:55.858 --> 12:57.067
Hey, Cute Guy!

12:57.151 --> 12:59.153
- Hello!
- Cute Guy!

12:59.236 --> 13:01.113
- Oh, you're right!
- It is Cute Guy!

13:01.197 --> 13:04.241
- Hello!
- Hi! How have you been?

13:04.742 --> 13:06.202
How have you been?

13:07.495 --> 13:09.413
What's going on?

13:09.497 --> 13:12.917
She got kicked out, so I told her
about the room. Good work, right?

13:13.918 --> 13:16.086
- Hey!
- Hey, Cute Guy!

13:17.797 --> 13:20.925
- I-ra, coming here was a great choice!
- Hey, Cute Guy!

13:24.595 --> 13:27.598
Hey, it's Lee Doona from Dream Sweet.

13:27.681 --> 13:29.809
- Hello.
- Hey, it's Lee Doona.

13:29.892 --> 13:31.727
- Hello.
- Hello.

13:33.187 --> 13:34.063
She's pretty.

13:34.897 --> 13:36.649
- She's so pretty.
- She's really pretty.

13:36.732 --> 13:37.775
- So pretty!
- It's Doona.

13:37.858 --> 13:38.692
Won-jun.

13:40.986 --> 13:41.821
Look at her.

13:46.492 --> 13:47.660
She got here fast.

13:55.751 --> 13:56.585
Thank you.

14:01.799 --> 14:04.593
She left home, so I told her to come.
Good work, right?

14:04.677 --> 14:05.845
- Hello.
- Hello.

14:12.101 --> 14:14.436
- Hey, Yun-taek!
- Could you take this?

14:14.520 --> 14:16.313
- Put it there.
- No!

14:16.397 --> 14:18.107
Yun-taek, put it here!

14:18.190 --> 14:20.192
- Hey!
- Don't put it there!

14:20.276 --> 14:21.527
It looks better here.

14:21.610 --> 14:23.153
- No!
- Just leave it here for now.

14:23.237 --> 14:25.197
- No, let go!
- This is better.

14:25.281 --> 14:26.574
Let's leave it here for now.

14:27.199 --> 14:28.784
Won-jun! Wait for me!

14:28.868 --> 14:31.787
What on earth are you wearing?
Aren't those pajamas?

14:31.871 --> 14:32.746
Aren't they cute?

14:32.830 --> 14:36.458
I treated my roomies to the same ones
as a housewarming gift.

14:37.459 --> 14:40.379
- Do you want a pair too?
- I'll pass, thanks.

14:40.462 --> 14:42.006
I know you want them.

14:45.467 --> 14:46.844
- Hey.
- What?

14:47.636 --> 14:49.096
What's she like? Doona, I mean.

14:50.306 --> 14:51.348
Shouldn't you call her Unni?

14:51.432 --> 14:54.184
Why would I?
We're the same age.

14:54.268 --> 14:57.313
Give me some intel!
I have to live with her now.

14:58.063 --> 14:59.773
What kind of person is Doona?

15:00.858 --> 15:02.276
I have no idea myself

15:03.068 --> 15:04.570
what goes on in her head.

15:11.035 --> 15:13.787
I'm back! Come here.

15:16.373 --> 15:17.541
Oh, you bought beer.

15:17.625 --> 15:19.752
Let's drink ourselves stupid!

15:19.835 --> 15:21.128
- Give me one.
- Sure.

15:21.211 --> 15:23.380
This is heavy.
How did you carry this here alone?

15:23.464 --> 15:24.715
I found a servant upstairs.

15:25.299 --> 15:27.009
Why? You want to come in too?

15:27.635 --> 15:29.762
- No.
- I wasn't going to let you in anyway.

15:29.845 --> 15:31.805
You're an outcast now! Good night!

15:32.306 --> 15:35.351
- So, then you must know Kooksu too?
- Of course!

15:35.434 --> 15:36.268
Really?

15:36.352 --> 15:38.604
He's inherited the business,
and he's now the CEO!

15:38.687 --> 15:41.106
No way! That lucky so-and-so!

15:41.190 --> 15:43.275
- You're annoyed!
- I'm really annoyed!

15:43.359 --> 15:45.861
- His name is Kooksu?
- His name is Su-jin!

15:45.945 --> 15:47.446
Jinx!

15:49.198 --> 15:50.658
Kook Su-jin, right?

15:50.741 --> 15:53.661
- Yup. Kooksu is really funny.
- Yeah, he really is.

15:54.203 --> 15:56.455
Then you must also know Happy Pharmacy?

15:56.538 --> 15:57.957
Of course! It's still there!

15:58.040 --> 15:59.625
- It's still there?
- Yes!

16:00.125 --> 16:02.169
- Oh, that place!
- What about it?

16:02.252 --> 16:04.880
Kook Su-jin used to have a crush
on the owner's daughter,

16:04.964 --> 16:07.216
so he'd always go there
to get an energy drink

16:07.299 --> 16:09.009
and ended up getting addicted to it.

16:09.093 --> 16:13.138
And since Won-jun was always with him,
he got addicted too!

16:13.222 --> 16:16.642
The two idiots walked around
like this all the time.

16:31.532 --> 16:33.450
Why are you coming outside?

16:33.534 --> 16:35.202
I-ra's on the phone with her mom.

16:45.671 --> 16:47.840
It must be hard
to suddenly live with others.

16:50.175 --> 16:54.138
I've lived in dorms for a long time.
It must be more uncomfortable for you.

16:56.306 --> 16:58.100
It feels like a school trip. It's fun.

16:59.560 --> 17:00.477
School trip?

17:01.520 --> 17:03.939
I've never been on one of those.

17:06.066 --> 17:08.527
Let's go on one sometime, the three of us.

17:08.610 --> 17:09.778
In school uniform.

17:11.530 --> 17:12.406
Sounds good.

17:24.251 --> 17:25.461
Why did you

17:26.712 --> 17:28.839
suddenly decide to get roommates?

17:29.965 --> 17:30.883
What about you?

17:32.384 --> 17:34.303
Why did you suddenly leave home?

17:34.928 --> 17:36.513
The timing was right.

17:38.015 --> 17:40.142
All those things that had gone wrong

17:41.852 --> 17:43.979
and all those things
that had piled up over time

17:44.772 --> 17:49.860
exploding due to something utterly trivial
in one crucial moment.

17:49.943 --> 17:51.445
I think that's what happened.

17:53.781 --> 17:55.157
In more ways than one.

18:00.287 --> 18:02.539
It's also why I told Won-jun
how I felt about him.

18:05.250 --> 18:06.919
- Did you?
- Yes.

18:07.920 --> 18:09.963
Not in so many words,

18:10.923 --> 18:12.549
but he probably understood.

18:18.555 --> 18:20.974
I've come here to hear his response.

18:22.643 --> 18:25.479
- I don't want to lose him this time.
- That's unfortunate.

18:29.066 --> 18:30.943
I can offer you a room,

18:32.820 --> 18:34.655
but I can't root for you in that regard.

18:36.198 --> 18:38.033
Because I've gotten myself involved too.

18:50.170 --> 18:51.004
Doona…

18:55.008 --> 18:56.426
I know Won-jun well.

18:57.553 --> 18:59.429
He always overthinks things,

19:01.557 --> 19:04.518
and he's cautious about everything,
almost to the point of excess.

19:05.602 --> 19:07.437
He doesn't get involved in anything

19:07.938 --> 19:10.983
unstable and precarious,
things that are certain to burn him.

19:11.817 --> 19:15.112
He and I have known each other
for a long time. We were very close.

19:16.488 --> 19:17.948
And had feelings for each other.

19:21.160 --> 19:22.703
That's very special too.

19:28.083 --> 19:31.211
We're late! Let's make a run for it!
I have a lecture in first period!

19:31.295 --> 19:34.423
- No!
- We're going to be late anyway.

19:34.506 --> 19:35.507
Your girlfriend.

19:35.591 --> 19:38.051
- Let's take a taxi. My bag's so heavy.
- It's hot!

19:38.135 --> 19:40.429
- We'll be late even by taxi.
- What's with all this?

19:40.512 --> 19:43.515
Get lost unless you're going to
carry it for me. Here! Let's go.

19:44.183 --> 19:45.392
What's your problem?

19:45.475 --> 19:49.146
- You jerk! What's wrong with you?
- Let's get something to eat first.

19:49.229 --> 19:50.772
That's very special too.

19:52.107 --> 19:53.233
Being familiar,

19:54.943 --> 19:56.612
having shared memories,

19:57.362 --> 19:59.489
living in the same world.

20:00.949 --> 20:02.284
That's powerful too.

20:05.412 --> 20:07.164
That's what I'm putting my faith in.

20:08.373 --> 20:10.667
- Hey!
- We should eat first.

20:10.751 --> 20:13.086
- That hurts!
- What's wrong? Are you all right?

20:13.754 --> 20:15.881
Hold on! Sorry!

20:15.964 --> 20:17.090
Seriously!

20:17.174 --> 20:18.634
- Come on!
- Get a move on!

20:19.134 --> 20:21.720
- Hey!
- Come on, let's eat first!

20:23.472 --> 20:24.598
Hey! Won-jun!

20:30.103 --> 20:33.690
How's it going with the celebrity?
Are you friends yet? What's she like?

20:33.774 --> 20:35.108
How should I put it?

20:35.192 --> 20:36.860
She's got a reputation.

20:36.944 --> 20:39.279
I'm not sure.
She's just like everyone else.

20:39.363 --> 20:41.740
Then how about the guys?

20:48.413 --> 20:49.665
What's that face for?

20:49.748 --> 20:53.001
What's going on with your nostrils?
What is it? You're scaring me.

21:00.425 --> 21:01.718
Actually,

21:03.178 --> 21:04.263
this morning…

21:04.346 --> 21:05.514
- Yeah?
- Yeah?

21:14.314 --> 21:15.816
MEN
CLOSE THE CURTAIN BEFORE SHOWERING

21:41.800 --> 21:43.468
I-ra Choi!

21:45.679 --> 21:48.640
- Marry him!
- Marry him!

21:48.724 --> 21:50.225
- Marry him!
- Marry him!

21:57.858 --> 21:59.318
It gave me butterflies.

22:02.487 --> 22:05.324
And I don't want to feel that way
over something meaningless.

23:15.435 --> 23:18.271
Be careful around people.
Because it shows.

23:21.691 --> 23:22.651
What shows?

23:24.945 --> 23:25.779
Your loneliness.

23:28.698 --> 23:31.034
Your desperation for love
to compensate for the lack of it.

23:31.868 --> 23:33.954
Your anxiousness
over losing people's interest.

23:43.088 --> 23:47.092
- The samba girl, I-ra Choi!
- The kissing king, Yun-taek!

23:51.555 --> 23:52.931
Why are you so hyped?

23:55.684 --> 23:57.769
- Thanks for cooking.
- Sure.

23:58.270 --> 24:01.231
- Would you like any help?
- No need. I'm all done.

24:04.234 --> 24:05.777
Do you have a blanket I could use?

24:05.861 --> 24:08.613
Oh, there's one in my bedroom,
on the chair.

24:10.574 --> 24:11.533
Okay. Thank you.

24:28.592 --> 24:30.302
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

25:31.947 --> 25:32.822
Have you found it?

25:33.448 --> 25:34.282
Yes!

25:37.160 --> 25:39.412
- Then come out for some beer.
- Sure.

25:58.723 --> 26:01.059
Wasn't that a celebrity?
Did I just gasp too loudly?

26:03.603 --> 26:05.564
She's from Dream Sweet!

26:22.163 --> 26:23.873
- You know me, right?
- Huh?

26:25.375 --> 26:26.334
Lee Doona!

26:37.220 --> 26:38.388
What an honor.

26:38.471 --> 26:41.474
A celebrity recognizing someone
who's just an old idol trainee.

26:42.809 --> 26:45.312
I don't know.
It's good to see a familiar face.

26:45.395 --> 26:47.897
A bit like meeting a fellow Korean
in a foreign country.

26:49.065 --> 26:51.693
You're even prettier than before.
What are you up to now?

26:52.277 --> 26:53.153
Nothing.

26:55.196 --> 26:58.158
It's a shame. What were you thinking?
You were doing well.

26:59.409 --> 27:02.370
- Well, I screwed it all up.
- Yeah.

27:02.871 --> 27:06.625
I feel like I could put up
with any shit thrown my way once I debut,

27:07.208 --> 27:10.003
but then I'm told
there's always new shit that comes up.

27:10.837 --> 27:12.213
It must have been tough.

27:16.509 --> 27:19.137
- Do you want to go somewhere else?
- Why not?

27:20.096 --> 27:21.473
People are, you know,

27:22.557 --> 27:27.687
designed to instinctively recognize others
that are similar to themselves.

27:27.771 --> 27:30.273
- Take I-ra Choi here, for example.
- Yes!

27:30.357 --> 27:32.776
The moment I saw her, I knew right away

27:32.859 --> 27:36.154
that she was totally my kind of person.

27:36.237 --> 27:38.365
- That's so nice!
- Totally my kind of person.

27:38.865 --> 27:42.535
Jin-ju and Won-jun, it's exactly the same
for you guys, isn't it?

27:42.619 --> 27:45.497
Birds of a feather. Right?

27:53.922 --> 27:55.590
- Yay!
- Yay! Here.

27:55.674 --> 27:57.801
- The kissing king!
- The kissing king!

27:58.385 --> 28:00.053
- Seriously!
- Stop complaining.

28:00.136 --> 28:02.097
- I'm sorry.
- Do you want me to carry her?

28:02.180 --> 28:04.224
I'll carry her. You can…

28:04.307 --> 28:07.477
- Just open the door, will you?
- Okay.

28:08.103 --> 28:11.147
- Jeez, this girl is so weird.
- Hey, be quiet!

28:11.231 --> 28:12.148
Stop it!

28:12.649 --> 28:14.067
Do you want to go for a walk?

28:16.528 --> 28:17.570
Let's go.

28:42.220 --> 28:43.221
I want to do that.

29:09.038 --> 29:10.123
Leave it.

29:13.585 --> 29:14.544
It's broken.

29:21.718 --> 29:22.927
OUT OF ORDER!

29:23.011 --> 29:27.515
I thought I'd sooner die
than tell you about my family.

29:30.477 --> 29:31.561
I was really happy

29:33.313 --> 29:34.814
that day.

29:36.649 --> 29:40.361
The person I liked had told me
that he liked me.

29:52.832 --> 29:53.792
I like you.

29:56.169 --> 29:58.129
My heart felt like it was about to burst.

29:58.671 --> 30:00.632
I felt like I got everything
I ever wanted.

30:01.174 --> 30:03.134
I wanted to scream and shout,
I was so happy.

30:13.394 --> 30:16.314
There were so many things
I wanted to do with you.

30:18.983 --> 30:20.902
And it felt like all of it was possible.

30:22.612 --> 30:23.488
You!

30:24.072 --> 30:27.367
Write down on here
everything you got up to with the guy.

30:28.993 --> 30:31.830
I said, do it now! You bitch!

30:31.913 --> 30:34.666
Please, honey! Just stop!

30:41.923 --> 30:46.386
It was like falling out of a dream
and back to reality with a thud.

30:49.055 --> 30:51.975
The Kim Jin-ju that Won-jun liked,

30:52.475 --> 30:55.937
the one that was always cheerful,
smiling, and self-confident, was fake.

30:56.855 --> 30:59.524
The real me was the miserable person

31:00.400 --> 31:02.819
who lived with this mess of a family.

31:07.740 --> 31:09.742
I suddenly lost all courage.

31:17.709 --> 31:19.711
Don't you have anything
you want to tell me?

31:29.721 --> 31:30.680
I…

31:33.016 --> 31:34.559
really liked you a lot.

31:56.497 --> 32:00.293
I really liked you a lot.

32:02.879 --> 32:05.089
So much so
that I didn't want to see you again

32:05.632 --> 32:07.383
in case I fell for you like that again

32:08.384 --> 32:10.261
and ended up getting hurt.

32:12.221 --> 32:14.223
So much so that when we met again,

32:14.849 --> 32:19.896
I couldn't even tell whether I still had
those feelings for you or not.

32:22.523 --> 32:24.150
I wish I could have comforted you

32:24.233 --> 32:26.903
when you were going through a rough time.

32:28.279 --> 32:29.197
But now…

32:31.366 --> 32:33.159
too much time has passed.

32:34.535 --> 32:36.204
You could comfort me now.

32:37.705 --> 32:39.540
Comfort me. Please?

32:40.041 --> 32:43.419
Comfort me, support me,

32:45.171 --> 32:47.382
and like me, just like you did before.

32:53.805 --> 32:55.890
It's you and me we're talking about.

33:02.021 --> 33:02.855
I'm sorry.

33:04.774 --> 33:09.570
I asked you out on a walk
because I felt I needed to say sorry.

34:31.235 --> 34:32.111
Bye.

34:37.742 --> 34:40.328
What the fuck?
What do you think you're doing?

34:44.415 --> 34:45.708
Right.

34:46.459 --> 34:48.127
So this is how you mess with people.

34:48.211 --> 34:50.546
I've come across a lot of people
who can't stand you.

34:51.130 --> 34:52.507
Now I know why.

34:53.758 --> 34:55.259
Then get lost.

34:56.761 --> 34:58.346
Are you trying to get his attention?

35:03.935 --> 35:05.269
Park In-wook.

35:07.980 --> 35:11.943
Must suck for you though. It seems like
the man's cut you off for good.

35:15.613 --> 35:16.447
What's going on?

35:18.991 --> 35:20.118
Who the hell are you?

35:23.538 --> 35:25.665
Is this the kid
you've been hanging out with?

35:26.374 --> 35:27.375
You…

35:29.460 --> 35:31.337
- How old are you?
- Why? How old are you?

35:31.420 --> 35:32.839
What was that, you little shit?

35:33.965 --> 35:37.051
Hey! Let's go.
I left my phone in your car.

35:38.761 --> 35:40.263
I'll get it for you.

35:42.056 --> 35:43.182
Let's go.

35:45.977 --> 35:47.395
Unbelievable.

36:04.370 --> 36:06.038
- What are you doing?
- Are you a friend?

36:06.122 --> 36:06.998
What?

36:07.081 --> 36:09.500
I'm asking if you're a friend of Doona's.

36:12.753 --> 36:15.047
She doesn't have any friends.

36:17.633 --> 36:20.386
I'm in the same position as you. She…

36:22.889 --> 36:24.223
Why am I laughing about this?

36:24.307 --> 36:26.350
She's just throwing herself at anyone

36:26.434 --> 36:29.020
to grab the attention
of that asshole, Park In-wook.

36:29.103 --> 36:30.980
I know it's her habit to do that,

36:31.063 --> 36:33.482
but if I get picked, why not?
It's a free lunch, right?

36:36.986 --> 36:38.905
What? Are you going to punch me?

36:41.365 --> 36:42.742
Just get the hell out of here.

36:44.160 --> 36:46.996
Why? Do you think you're different?

36:47.955 --> 36:50.249
What, are you fucking in love with her?

36:55.421 --> 36:56.380
Fuck!

36:58.257 --> 36:59.091
Fuck!

37:00.384 --> 37:01.552
You son of a…

37:37.171 --> 37:39.507
What goes on in that mind of yours?

37:44.345 --> 37:45.888
I'm dying to know.

38:52.371 --> 38:55.583
It's okay to get butterflies from me.
Everyone does and then gets over it.

38:56.167 --> 38:57.543
You think you're any different?

39:12.141 --> 39:13.476
What are you doing here?

39:31.952 --> 39:34.330
Have you been exercising?
You're covered in sweat.

39:41.295 --> 39:44.090
What? Is this off-limits too?

39:47.343 --> 39:48.719
Butterflies again?

39:55.851 --> 39:56.811
This is hard.

40:20.835 --> 40:21.669
Hey!

40:46.402 --> 40:48.070
Can I ask you something?

40:51.198 --> 40:53.159
You said I'm no different. To who?

40:53.826 --> 40:55.911
The guy from tonight? No? Then who?

40:58.956 --> 41:00.124
Perhaps you've forgotten?

41:01.333 --> 41:03.043
You said it was meaningless.

41:04.295 --> 41:05.921
Although I didn't deny it

41:06.005 --> 41:08.257
because you could be right.

41:11.427 --> 41:14.388
That's why I decided
to hang out with other people.

41:15.181 --> 41:16.348
I was curious, too…

41:18.434 --> 41:19.727
whether my feelings for you

41:20.811 --> 41:22.938
mean that I like you…

41:25.065 --> 41:27.109
or that I'm tired of being alone?

41:30.571 --> 41:32.531
But what will you do
if that's not the case?

41:34.575 --> 41:36.785
What if I'm surrounded by other people,

41:37.286 --> 41:40.623
but I still like you and still miss you?

41:43.876 --> 41:46.128
If it actually turns out
that I've fallen for you,

41:47.922 --> 41:49.465
what will you do then?

41:58.599 --> 41:59.475
See?

42:00.851 --> 42:02.520
You can't answer either, can you?

42:37.179 --> 42:38.889
You said you don't kiss your friends.

42:40.641 --> 42:41.517
I don't.

45:34.732 --> 45:39.737
Subtitle translation by: Reuben Simpson
